---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Product Prototypes & Mockups | Carve Model"
  description="Physical product prototypes and mockups — appearance models, form studies, functional prototypes, and investor demo pieces built from CAD, sketches, and reference images."
  canonicalPath="/scale-model-services/product"
  ogTitle="Product Prototypes & Mockups | Carve Model"
  ogDescription="Physical product prototypes and mockups — appearance models, form studies, functional prototypes, and investor demo pieces built from CAD, sketches, and reference images."
  active="services"
  imageSlot={true}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={`{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Service","serviceType":"Product Prototypes & Mockups","provider":{"@type":"ProfessionalService","name":"Carve Model","areaServed":["United States","Canada"]}}`} />
<style>
.breadcrumb{padding-top:1.6rem;}
.breadcrumb a{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);transition:color var(--dur-2);}
.breadcrumb a:hover{color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.page-hero{padding-top:1.6rem;padding-bottom:clamp(2.5rem,4vw,4rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.page-hero h1{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.page-hero p{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.hero__cta{display:flex;gap:0.9rem;flex-wrap:nowrap;margin-top:1.8rem;}
@media(max-width:560px){.hero__cta{flex-wrap:wrap;}}
.hero__cta .btn--primary,.hero__cta .btn--ghost{background:transparent;color:var(--cm-text-strong);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);}
.hero__cta .btn--primary:hover,.hero__cta .btn--ghost:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.dedi-media{margin-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);}
.dedi-media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:21/9;}
.dedi-body{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);}
.dedi-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);align-items:start;}
.dedi-grid h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.6vw,2.1rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;}
.dedi-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.4rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.8rem;}
.dedi-list li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.98rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.dedi-list li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
@media(max-width:820px){.dedi-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-section{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-section h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.3rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin-top:1rem;}
.svc-section .lead-p{margin-top:1.2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.8rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.75rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.98rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.svc-checklist li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
.svc-types{display:grid;gap:1.6rem;margin-top:2rem;}
.svc-type{padding-top:1.6rem;border-top:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-type:first-child{padding-top:0;border-top:0;}
.svc-type h3{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:var(--w-semibold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.svc-type p{margin-top:0.5rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;max-width:66ch;}
.svc-steps{display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.4rem 1fr;gap:1rem;padding-block:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-step:last-child{border-bottom:0;}
.svc-step__n{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);padding-top:0.15rem;}
.svc-step p{color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;}
.svc-note{margin-top:1.4rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);max-width:68ch;}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main>
<div class="container breadcrumb"><a href="/scale-model-services">← All services</a></div>

<section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Services / Product</span>
  <h1 class="display-lg measure">Turn a digital concept into a physical object you can evaluate.</h1>
  <p class="lead measure">Carve Model creates physical product prototypes and mockups from CAD files, drawings, sketches, reference images, renderings, and generated concepts.</p>
  <p class="muted measure">Our prototypes help product teams communicate form, evaluate proportion, review materials and finishes, demonstrate an idea, and prepare for further development or production.</p>
  <div class="hero__cta">
    <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/works">View Product Work <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="dedi-media"><image-slot id="svc-product-hero" placeholder="Drop product prototype photo" src="/assets/service-product-prototype-hero-v3.webp"></image-slot></div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Why build a physical prototype?</span>
  <h2>Some decisions require a real object.</h2>
  <p class="lead-p muted">A rendering or digital model can present an idea, but a physical prototype allows people to hold it, view it at its intended size, examine it from every angle, and understand how its components relate.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Depending on the project, a prototype can help teams:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Evaluate overall form and proportion</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Review ergonomics and handling</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Compare materials, colors, and finishes</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Communicate a concept to stakeholders or investors</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Study components, joints, and assembly</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Demonstrate a product at an event or presentation</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Identify questions before committing to production</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Create a physical reference for further development</li>
  </ul>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Prototype types</span>
  <h2>Built around what needs to be evaluated.</h2>
  <div class="svc-types">
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Appearance models</h3><p>High-quality physical representations focused on form, color, materials, finishes, and visual presentation. They may resemble the proposed final product without reproducing its complete internal function.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Form and proportion studies</h3><p>Simplified models used to evaluate size, shape, balance, ergonomics, and the relationship between major components.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Material and finish samples</h3><p>Physical samples developed to compare colors, textures, coatings, transparency, surface treatments, and transitions between materials.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Functional prototypes</h3><p>Prototypes that reproduce selected movements, connections, interactions, or operating features. The required functions are defined before production.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Assembly and connection mockups</h3><p>Models used to examine how components fit, connect, separate, move, or are assembled.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Presentation and demonstration models</h3><p>Refined prototypes for investor meetings, trade shows, product launches, internal presentations, and other environments where an idea must be understood quickly.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Enlarged or reduced models</h3><p>Products or components reproduced at a different scale to make small details easier to explain or large objects easier to present.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Appearance or function?</span>
  <h2>Define what the prototype must prove.</h2>
  <p class="lead-p muted">A single prototype does not always need to reproduce appearance, materials, assembly, and function at the same time.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Before production, we establish:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> What must look like the proposed product</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> What must match the intended dimensions</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> What needs to move or function</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> What can be simplified</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Which materials or finishes require confirmation</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> How the prototype will be handled or demonstrated</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Whether components need to be removable</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> What remains outside the prototype's intended purpose</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="svc-note">This prevents unnecessary complexity and focuses the scope on the decisions the prototype must support.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Start with what you have</span>
  <h2>From reference image to fabrication-ready geometry.</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">We can review:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> CAD and production files</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> 3D models</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Dimensioned drawings</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Engineering information</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Sketches and marked-up images</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Photographs and renderings</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Existing physical products</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Material references</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> AI-generated concept images</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="svc-note">When usable geometry exists, we prepare it for fabrication. When the project begins only with visual references or incomplete information, Digital Model Development may be separately scoped.</p>
  <p class="svc-note" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">The developed geometry and interpreted design decisions are reviewed before physical fabrication.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Materials and methods</span>
  <h2>Selected for the required outcome.</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Depending on the project, production may combine:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> 3D printing</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> CNC machining</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Laser cutting</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Acrylic, ABS, resin, wood, metal, or foam</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Painting and custom finishes</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Transparent or illuminated components</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Mechanical connections</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Removable or interchangeable parts</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Electronics and selected functional elements</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Skilled assembly and hand finishing</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="svc-note">Materials and methods are selected according to the prototype's purpose, appearance, accuracy, handling, schedule, and budget.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Important distinction</span>
  <h2>A prototype has a defined purpose.</h2>
  <p class="lead-p muted">A product mockup or prototype does not automatically certify manufacturing readiness, engineering performance, code compliance, safety, or durability.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;max-width:68ch;">Where those forms of validation are required, the appropriate engineering, testing, certification, or production specialists should also be involved.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.6rem;max-width:68ch;">Carve defines clearly what the prototype is intended to communicate or evaluate.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section" style="border-bottom:0;"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
  <h2>From concept to physical evidence.</h2>
  <div class="svc-steps">
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">01</span><p>Define the audience and evaluation objective</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">02</span><p>Confirm dimensions, functions, materials, and constraints</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">03</span><p>Review or develop the required digital geometry</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">04</span><p>Produce samples or partial mockups when useful</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">05</span><p>Approve key design decisions</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">06</span><p>Fabricate, assemble, finish, and test the defined features</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">07</span><p>Package and deliver the completed prototype</p></div>
  </div>
  <a class="svc-explore" href="/model-making-process" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;margin-top:1.4rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.82rem;letter-spacing:0.03em;color:var(--cm-text-strong);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);padding-bottom:2px;">View Our Process <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="cta reveal" style="position:relative;text-align:center;background:var(--cm-black);border:1px solid var(--cm-border);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem) var(--gutter);">
    <h2 class="display-md">Start a product prototype project.</h2>
    <p class="muted mt-2" style="max-width:52ch;margin-inline:auto;">Tell us what you are developing, what needs to be evaluated or demonstrated, and what information is currently available. We will recommend an appropriate prototype scope and production approach.</p>
    <div class="hero__cta" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:2.4rem;">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/scale-model-services">All services <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
